gamescope WSI layer: only advertise the extra HDR surface formats the driver
can back on the Gamescope surface.

The layer appends A2B10G10R10/A2R10G10B10 (HDR10) and R16G16B16A16 (scRGB)
to every Gamescope surface's format list, but CreateSwapchainKHR then
refuses any format the driver itself doesn't list for that surface. On
NVIDIA, a native game (Longshot) picked the advertised
A2R10G10B10 + HDR10_ST2084 and got VK_ERROR_INITIALIZATION_FAILED
("Refusing to make swapchain (unsupported VkFormat)"), so it never started.
With this, games only see the HDR formats that work (A2B10G10R10 there).

--- a/layer/VkLayer_FROG_gamescope_wsi.cpp	2026-11-26 21:16:13.409964894 -0500
+++ b/layer/VkLayer_FROG_gamescope_wsi.cpp	2026-11-26 21:16:31.719671884 -0500
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@
 #include <utility>
 #include <tuple>
 #include <vector>
+#include <array>
 #include <algorithm>
 #include <functional>
 #include <unordered_map>
@@ -1126,6 +1127,33 @@
